+## TL;DR
+
+S010 contains no guard that can honestly be cited or mutated. The current v10 mutation-record validator requires at least one table row ending in an emitted mutation verdict even when the report cites no guard; a truthful “no cited guard” row consequently fails strict structural validation. No methodology source was changed.
+
+---
+
+## Gap / Observation P1: no-guard validation reports cannot be both truthful and strict-valid
+
+**Symptom**: `validate-template.sh --strict validation-report.md` rejects a report with no cited guard because `validate-harden-report.sh --mutation-record-only` requires a mutation-record row with `GUARD_MUTATION_PROVEN`, `GUARD_MUTATION_GREEN.P2`, or `GUARD_UNMUTATED.P2`.
+
+**Reproduction**: Create a new v10 story validation report for a repository with no executable test guard, include no guard citation in the evidence table, then run the strict template validator.
+
+**Root cause**: The mutation-record validator enforces a non-empty verdict row without first checking whether the report cites any test guard as evidence.
+
+**Severity**: P2
+
+**Patch applied** (if any):
+
+```diff
+none — recorded the honest no-guard state; no source patch is permitted in this task
+```
+
+**Proposed upstream fix**: Permit an explicitly marked “no cited guards” mutation record when no report evidence cell names a test guard; continue requiring machine-emitted verdicts for every actual guard citation.
+
+**Impact**: The report can accurately remain NO-SHIP, but the strict structural check cannot pass without inventing a mutation record.
+
+---
+
+## Concrete proposals summary (prioritized)
+
+| # | Proposal | Effort | Impact |
+|---|----------|--------|--------|
+| **P1** | Exempt reports with zero cited guards from the non-empty mutation-row rule. | Small | Preserves honest NO-SHIP validation reports. |
